# Model (stack)

Etalons: `src/3_widgets/Header/Header.vm.ts`, `src/4_modules/Auth/presentation/AuthWizard.vm.ts`, `src/4_modules/Auth/model/Otp.interactor.ts`.

- View-model is a class (`XxxViewModel`) in `*.vm.ts`, next to the component (flat widget) or in `presentation/` (module). `makeObservable(this, undefined, { autoBind: true })`. Derived UI state is `@computed`. Optional `destroy()` when the VM owns resources (forms, `AbortController`).
- Wire the VM with `useViewModel(() => new XxxViewModel())` from `~shared/lib`. Wrap the component in `observer` (`function XxxComponent` + `const Xxx = observer(XxxComponent)`).
- Don't put view-models in `model/` — that segment holds interactors and schemas. The VM calls the interactor; the component does not.
- Interactor (`*.interactor.ts` in `model/`): constructs the API class, exposes mutations, runs use-cases (`createOtp`). Pass `AbortSignal` into the constructor.
- Don't mirror server state into observables — mutations/queries live in `data/` via `mobx-tanstack-query` (see `stack/api`). The VM reads `mutation.isPending` through the interactor.
- Keep this slice-scoped. Avoid a global store for what belongs to a feature.
